3.1 Copying and killing
=======================

‘M-w’ and ‘C-w’ act on the selections while there are any, and behave as
usual when there are none.  You don't have to think about it.

   Copied pieces are joined with a newline.  For a different separator
just this once, use ‘C-u C-c M w’ and type it.  To change it for good,
set ‘multi-region-separator’.

   Copying deselects everything, so you can start fresh.  Set
‘multi-region-keep-after-copy’ to keep the selections instead.

   A word that a PDF split with a ‘¬’ is joined again: "inflam¬ mation"
is copied as "inflammation".


File: multi-region.info,  Node: Changing all selections at once,  Next: Moving between selections,  Prev: Copying and killing,  Up: Using the selections

3.2 Changing all selections at once
===================================

‘C-c M r’ asks for a text and puts it in place of every selection.

   ‘C-c M x’ asks for a command and runs it on each selection as if it
were the region.  Good ones to try: ‘upcase-region’, ‘comment-region’,
‘fill-region’.

   ‘C-/’ (undo) puts the text back after either, and after ‘C-w’.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: Moving between selections,  Next: Deselecting and bringing back,  Prev: Changing all selections at once,  Up: Using the selections

3.3 Moving between selections
=============================

‘C-c M n’ and ‘C-c M p’ move point to the next and previous selection.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: Deselecting and bringing back,  Prev: Moving between selections,  Up: Using the selections

3.4 Deselecting and bringing back
=================================

‘C-c M u’ deselects the selection you made last.  ‘C-c M c’ deselects
everything.

   ‘C-c M /’ brings back what was last deselected all at once, whether
by ‘C-c M c’, by copying, or by ‘C-g’ in a PDF or EPUB.  Selections you
made since are kept.

   It works after changing the text too:

   • after ‘C-c M r’, it selects the replacements, so you can carry on
     with them;
   • after ‘C-w’, undo first (‘C-/’) to put the text back, then ‘C-c M
     /’ selects it again.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: Pictures,  Next: In each kind of buffer,  Prev: Using the selections,  Up: Top

4 Pictures
**********

A picture in the buffer is selected whole or not at all.  Drag across it
with the text around it, or ‘C-click’ it to select it alone.  A selected
picture gets a band in the selection color; ‘multi-region-image-margin’
sets its width, and 0 turns it off.

   This works for pictures in eww and EPUBs, and for inline images in
Org (‘C-c C-x C-v’) and Markdown (‘C-c C-x C-i’).  In Org and Markdown,
a link to a picture file counts even when the picture isn't shown.

   Copying takes only the text.  The pictures are for packages that
build notes from your selections, such as readq; see *note For other
packages: For other packages.


