5.1 Text, Org, Markdown and code
================================

Everything in this manual works.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: eww and other read-only buffers,  Next: EPUB books,  Prev: Text Org Markdown and code,  Up: In each kind of buffer

5.2 eww and other read-only buffers
===================================

Selecting, copying, jumping and deselecting work.  Killing, replacing
and running a command stop with "Buffer is read-only", as they would for
an ordinary region (killing copies first).

   On a link, ‘C-drag’ selects.  A ‘C-click’ that selects nothing still
opens the link in a new window, as usual.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: EPUB books,  Next: PDFs (pdf-tools),  Prev: eww and other read-only buffers,  Up: In each kind of buffer

5.3 EPUB books
==============

In books opened with nov.el, selections are remembered for each chapter
and come back when you return to it.  Copying collects them from all
chapters, in reading order.  ‘C-g’ deselects everything in every
chapter.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: PDFs (pdf-tools),  Next: PDFs (pdf-canvas),  Prev: EPUB books,  Up: In each kind of buffer

5.4 PDFs (pdf-tools)
====================

A PDF page is a picture, so there is no point to move: you select with
the mouse.

Mouse       What it does
----------------------------------------------------------
drag        Start over with a new selection on the page
‘C-drag’    Add another selection
click       Nothing: the selections stay
‘M-drag’    Select a picture area, such as a figure
‘M-click’   Deselect the picture area under the pointer

   Selections are remembered for each page, and copying collects them
from all pages.  ‘C-g’ deselects everything on every page.

   Copy, deselect last, deselect all and bring back work as in text.
Kill, replace, run-command and next/previous don't apply; ‘C-w’ copies
instead of killing.

   Highlights follow ‘pdf-view-selection-style’, so what you see is
exactly what is copied.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: PDFs (pdf-canvas),  Prev: PDFs (pdf-tools),  Up: In each kind of buffer

5.5 PDFs (pdf-canvas)
=====================

pdf-canvas keeps several selections itself, on any number of pages
(drag, then ‘C-drag’; ‘M-drag’ for a picture area).  multi-region gives
them the same commands as in a pdf-tools buffer, and ‘C-g’ remembers
what it deselects, so ‘C-c M /’ can bring it back.


