6 Options
*********

Change these with ‘M-x customize-group RET multi-region’, or with ‘setq’
in your init file.

‘multi-region-separator’
     What goes between copied pieces.  A newline by default.
‘multi-region-keep-after-copy’
     Keep the selections after copying.  Off by default.
‘multi-region-thing’
     What ‘C-c M SPC’ selects at point: ‘word’ (the default), ‘symbol’,
     ‘sentence’, ‘line’, or anything ‘thing-at-point’ knows.
‘multi-region-image-margin’
     Width in pixels of the band around selected pictures.  4 by
     default; 0 for none.
‘multi-region-prefix-key’
     The key that leads to the commands.  ‘C-c M’ by default; see *note
     Other keys: Other keys.
‘multi-region-ignored-modes’
     Major modes where ‘global-multi-region-mode’ stays off, so that
     C-drag keeps its own meaning there: Dired, Magit, Ibuffer and
     terminal buffers by default.  ‘M-x multi-region-mode’ still turns
     it on in one of them.
‘multi-region-face’
     How selections look.  Like the region, by default.

