6.1 Other keys
==============

To use ‘C-c s’ as the prefix instead of ‘C-c M’:

     (setopt multi-region-prefix-key "C-c s")

   ‘setopt’ needs Emacs 29.  On older versions, use ‘M-x
customize-option RET multi-region-prefix-key’, or ‘setq’ it _before_
multi-region is loaded; a ‘setq’ afterwards does nothing.  Set it to
‘nil’ for no prefix at all, and bind the commands in
‘multi-region-command-map’ to keys of your own.

   To select with ‘M-S-drag’ instead of ‘C-drag’:

     (define-key multi-region-mode-map [C-down-mouse-1] nil)
     (define-key multi-region-mode-map [M-S-down-mouse-1] #'multi-region-mouse-drag)


File: multi-region.info,  Node: For other packages,  Next: When pdf-tools is updated,  Prev: Options,  Up: Top

7 For other packages
********************

‘(multi-region-selections &optional absorb)’ returns the selections of
the current buffer in reading order, without changing them.  With
‘absorb’, an active region becomes a selection first.  Each selection is
a property list:

   • in text: ‘(:beg BEG :end END :text TEXT)’;
   • in an EPUB, also ‘:chapter’, the chapter number;
   • with pictures, also ‘:images’, each ‘(:beg BEG :end END :file
     FILE)’, or ‘:data’ and ‘:type’ for a picture that is not in a file;
   • in a PDF: ‘(:page PAGE :edges (LEFT TOP RIGHT BOTTOM) :text TEXT)’,
     edges as fractions of the page.  A picture area also has ‘:figure
     t’ and empty text.

   ‘(multi-region-clear)’ deselects everything.


File: multi-region.info,  Node: When pdf-tools is updated,  Next: Command index,  Prev: For other packages,  Up: Top

8 When pdf-tools is updated
***************************

multi-region relies on a few details of how pdf-tools works inside.
They are all in one file, ‘multi-region-pdf-tools.el’, listed at its
top.  After updating pdf-tools, run this in multi-region's folder:

     make test-pdf-tools

   If something no longer holds, the test says which, for example
"breaks assumption 2 in multi-region-pdf-tools.el".  Until it is fixed,
PDF selections may not draw or copy correctly; text and EPUB buffers are
not affected.


